<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Maceio port not affected by strike.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Maceio port not affected by strike.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian sugar port of Maceio did not join a national strike by stevedores on Friday because there were no vessels docked there, union officials said.</p>
<p>&quot;We are not striking because there are no ships at the port,&quot; said an official at the Maceio Stevedores' Union.</p>
<p>The strike has stopped operations at the ports of Santos, Vitorio and Rio de Janeiro. Loading was unaffected at Recife while Paranagua will halt work for one hour at 1600 GMT, which will not affect grain loading at the export terminal.</p>
<p>--Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsroom +55 11 248 5417</p>
